  "body": "When processing `referrer`-named `<meta>` tags, we're still looking out for and [adapting to legacy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#meta-referrer) referrer policy values. We're [considering](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=844322) dropping support for legacy referrer policy keywords in Chrome, and will be collecting data on this soon to see exactly how feasible this is.\r\n\r\nIt seems that the only mention of the legacy/[unknown](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-referrer-policy/#unknown-policy-values) referrer policy keywords in the HTML Standard are in this meta referrer section, and since Chrome actually supports the legacy referrer policy keywords on several HTML elements apart from `<meta>`, we may be dropping support _in that_ context regardless. With this in mind, I'm filing this to see if I can roust some support for this by the editors and/or perhaps other referrer policy implementers (@mcmanus for Firefox) to gauge interest and preliminary feasibility before we have sufficient data to back anything.\r\n\r\n/cc @jeisinger @estark37 ",
